I have a different method for IDing wands. The engraving thing just did 
not work for me; and is not really all that enlightening.

Now I zap unidentified wands at the closest mold, fungus, floating eye, 
spore, quivering blob, or jelly. Charges from attack wands are not 
wasted on creating permanent marks on the floor. Yes, polymorph can be 
somewhat dangerous; had a large mimic turn into a xorn once. Wands of 
make invisible can be indistiguishable from wands of teleport; but a 
couple of thrown daggers sorts that out.
  But lines such as:
"The floating eye slows down"
"The floating eye speeds up"
are just too humourous.


